This is the DVD plugin for the Video Disk Recorder (VDR).

Project's homepage:
    https://github.com/vdr-projects/vdr-plugin-dvd

Written by:
    Andreas Schultz <aschultz@warp10.net> (original author)
    Sven Göthel (interim maintainer)
    Marco Schlüssler, Miko Wohlgemuth (CVS team)
    Dirk Nehring <dnehring@gmx.net> (modernization)

Currently community maintained on the project's homepage.

See the file COPYING for license information.


Requirements
============

VDR       >= 2.6.6   https://www.tvdr.de/
libdvdnav >= 5.0.0   https://www.videolan.org/developers/libdvdnav.html
liba52    >= 0.7.4   https://sourceforge.net/projects/liba52/
libdvdcss (optional) https://www.videolan.org/developers/libdvdcss.html

Tested with VDR 2.8.3, libdvdnav 7.0.0, libdvdread 7.0.1, libdvdcss 1.5.0
and liba52 0.7.4. VDR versions before 2.6.6 are no longer supported.

Build and install the plugin like any other VDR plugin. The Makefile links
with -ldvdnav and -la52, so the development files of both libraries must be
installed.

libdvdcss is needed for CSS encrypted discs only. libdvdread, which
libdvdnav uses, loads it at runtime; the plugin doesn't link with it.
Check whether the law of your country allows its use.


DVD drive
=========

The plugin reads from /dev/cdrom, the link udev creates for the first
drive (/dev/sr0), unless another device is given with -C:

    vdr -P"dvd -C /dev/sr1"

-C also takes an ISO image of a DVD. If the device or image given with -C
doesn't exist yet, the plugin logs it and VDR starts anyway; a USB drive
can be plugged in later.

The user VDR runs as needs access to the drive. On most distributions that
means being a member of the "cdrom" group.


Audio
=====

With VDR 2.8.3 and newer, the plugin passes the disc's audio (AC-3, DTS,
LPCM, MPEG) to the output device as it is, and the device decodes it. With
older VDR versions and "Use Dolby Digital" off in VDR's setup, the plugin
decodes AC-3 itself with liba52; DTS is not played then.


Keys during playback
====================

Play, Up          play
Pause, Down       pause
FastFwd, Right    fast forward, slow motion forward while paused
FastRew, Left     fast rewind, slow motion backward while paused
                  (speeds as in VDR's own replay, see "Multi speed mode")
Red               jump to a time: enter hours and minutes (hh:mm), then
                  Ok to jump there (Down: and pause), or Left/Right to
                  jump that far backward/forward
Green             1 minute backward
Yellow            1 minute forward
Blue              go to a title: enter its number, then Ok
Ok                show/hide the progress display (subtitles are hidden
                  while it is open)
Back, Stop        stop replay
Audio             VDR's audio track menu
Subtitles         VDR's subtitle menu
2                 next subtitle stream, after the last one subtitles off
3                 next camera angle
4, Prev           previous chapter
6, Next           next chapter
7, ChanDn         previous title
9, ChanUp         next title
5                 DVD navigation mode (see below); with the progress
                  display open: the disc's root menu
8                 the disc's title menu
0                 the disc's audio menu

Next and previous title step through the disc's title numbers and wrap
around at the ends. Blue also reaches titles the disc's menus don't offer.


Keys in DVD menus
=================

In the disc's menus and in DVD navigation mode:

Up, Down, Left, Right,
2, 8, 4, 6        select a button
Ok, 5             activate the selected button
1                 root menu
3                 title menu
7                 subtitle menu
9, 0              audio menu
Green, Yellow     previous, next title
Red               leave DVD navigation mode

Blue and Back work as during playback.

Some discs (games, quizzes) expect button input outside their menus. Key 5
switches to DVD navigation mode for them, Red switches back.


Setup
=====

Preferred menu language      the languages the disc should choose for
Preferred audio language     its menus, audio and subtitles, if it has
Preferred subtitle language  them (default: en)
Player region code           region 1-8 reported to the disc, 0 keeps
                             libdvdnav's default (default: 2)
Display subtitles            show subtitles a disc switches on by itself
                             (default: no); subtitles chosen with key 2,
                             VDR's subtitle menu or the disc's menu are
                             always shown
Hide Mainmenu Entry          hide "DVD" in VDR's main menu
ReadAHead                    libdvdnav's read-ahead cache (default: no)
Gain (analog)                volume of AC-3 audio the plugin decodes
                             itself, see "Audio" (0-10, default: 4)


Resume
======

When replay stops inside a title, the plugin stores the title, chapter and
position of the disc in the file dvdplayer.resume in VDR's video directory
("make RESUMEDIR=..." sets another directory). The next replay of the same
disc continues 30 seconds before that position.


Known issue
===========

With subtitles on, the progress display can disappear while the plugin
still considers it open. Press Ok once more to close it for real.
